# Quest 3S Performance Budget

## Target

- **72 FPS** sustained on Meta Quest 3S
- Frame time budget: ~13.9ms total (CPU + GPU)

## Rendering

- URP with baked lighting where possible; limit realtime lights to 1 key light per scene
- Enable LOD on imported meshes (conveyor, electrical panel, environment)
- Occlusion culling for industrial scenes
- Avoid transparent overdraw on HUD — use opaque panels with alpha clip if needed

## Scripts

- No empty `Update()` loops — use events, coroutines, or XRI callbacks
- Object pool for frequently spawned feedback (cones, tags, particles)
- Cache `ControlCenter.Instance` references in Start, not per-frame

## VR comfort

- Fixed timestep interactions; debounce button presses
- Limit haptic pulses to 100–200ms
- No camera shake on safety alerts — use audio + UI instead

## Build

- Android IL2CPP, ARM64
- Strip unused XRI/MR sample assets from player builds (already excluded via folders)
- Test on device early each slice — Editor XR Simulator is not sufficient for perf sign-off

## ALWAYS

1. Profile with Meta XR Tools before marking slice complete
2. Batch static environment geometry
3. Use texture atlases for UI sprites where practical

## NEVER

1. Import high-poly Sketchfab assets without decimation/LOD
2. Use `FindObjectOfType` in Update
3. Enable full-scene realtime GI in simulation scenes
